iew with Rolling  Stones glick soul bioshock creator ken  Levine discussed the series of events  that drove him away from the iconic  franchise apart from logistical matters  that led to Levine studio irrational  being shuttered the designer also shared  personal reasons for leaving Bioshock  behind as Levine says development on  bioshock infinite had an adverse effect  on his life from his personal  relationships to his own health when  asked about his decision to move on to  other creative pursuits he said I think  the natural expectation was that I would  go and do the next bigger and  her bio shot game and I felt I think  I'll fail if I do that I think I'll lose  my mind and my marriage and so my  solution was to quit and what's probably  the weirdest news story of the week the  tail is emerge of a Miami man who  received an xbox one two weeks before  the console was ever even announced  apparently 25 year old Jiali had ordered  a new laptop and instead received a  prototype Xbox one that was stored at  the same shipping facility whether it  was a shipping label error or a problem  with Microsoft back-end Lee opened the  package to find a machine the general  public wouldn't even see for another two  weeks Microsoft soon sent a  representative to retrieve the console  and cover up the incident in what we  like to think was a men in black style  operation lady and gentlemen if you will  look right here so there you have it the  top 5 news stories from this week  between the updates to Pokemon go  resident evil 7 biohazard and your ps4  you should have plenty to keep you busy  until jess mcdonald is back here doing  top 5 next week until then
 

